.EXT. CITIES AROUND THE WORLD - DAY TO SUNSET #S01#

[[SH010 | 2 | WIDE, high | Handheld, phone-camera feel | The film opens here, cold. SH010 to SH110: random riot shots, different cities and countries, no order. Multi-shot generations | ]]

A crowd fills an avenue from wall to wall. Above the heads, signs with the same old face: devil horns drawn on, the eyes crossed out in red, one printout of him photoshopped hanging from a noose.

NEWS ANCHORS (V.O.)
(overlapping, many accents, over SH010 to SH110)
...protests in more than forty countries... ...the index lost another eleven percent... ...fuel up again overnight...

[[SH020 | 2 | MEDIUM | Locked-off | Numbers per liter, no currency sign. Precedent: Nigeria 2023, petrol about 3x overnight | ]]

A gas station. A worker on a ladder pulls 1.94 off the price board and slides in 5.89. Under it, DIESEL already reads 6.31. A line of cars. Nobody honks.

[[SH030 | 4 | WIDE, long lens | Handheld | Distance: nothing explicit | ]]

A police line. Hands pull a POLICEMAN into the crowd by his vest. Another officer drags him back. A pistol rises above the heads and fires. The police fire back. Everyone scatters.

[[SH040 | 1 | INSERT | Locked-off | | ]]

A cardboard sign. His face. A red X over each eye.

[[SH050 | 2 | WIDE | Handheld | PROPOSED | ]]

A billboard of his smiling face burns, the paper curling off in sheets.

[[SH060 | 2 | MEDIUM WIDE | Handheld | | ]]

A wall of riot shields. A bottle of fire bursts against it. Flames run down the shields. The line breaks.

[[SH070 | 2 | WIDE, long lens | Locked-off | | ]]

A highway out of a city, jammed. Mattresses tied on car roofs.

[[SH080 | 2 | MEDIUM, low | Handheld | PROPOSED | ]]

A tear gas canister skids across the asphalt, spinning, pouring white smoke. Feet run past it.

[[SH090 | 1 | CLOSE | Locked-off | | ]]

A child's face at a car window.

[[SH100 | 2 | WIDE | Locked-off | | ]]

A police truck stands abandoned, windows smashed. A bottle sails through the broken windshield. Fire fills the cab.

[[SH110 | 3 | EXTREME WIDE | Slow pan | | ]]

Sunset. A skyline under columns of smoke. Sirens far away.

[[SH120 | 9 | MEDIUM, a TV in a shop window | Locked-off | Professional news graphics. His clean face on screen | ]]

A television behind a cracked shop window. A news channel: a polished logo, a red BREAKING bar, a ticker of red numbers. In the corner, his official portrait: the same old face, clean, smiling. A REPORTER, sexy, every hair in place, on a rooftop with smoke behind her.

REPORTER
His location is still unknown. Authorities are warning the locals that any harm to this man will have serious repercussions.

SMASH CUT TO:

.EXT. DUSTY ROAD INTO A TOWN - DAY #S02#

[[SH010 | 4 | EXTREME WIDE | Locked-off | Hard cut to silence. Hold it. The outer towers stand shoulder to shoulder like a wall (look/mood/mood_4_town-edge.webp) | Towers, not a wall]]

Silence. A dry, dusty town on the edge of the desert, its outer towers standing shoulder to shoulder like a wall. The sun on the rooftops.

[[SH020 | 3 | MEDIUM | Locked-off | One generation with SH040: the dog lying, then its head lifting in close-up. PROPOSED: a lean street dog, short sandy coat, upright ears, curled tail | One take with SH040]]

A stray dog lies in the shadow of an abandoned building, on the edge of a crumbled concrete wall. Heat rises off the ground.

[[SH030 | 5 | EXTREME WIDE, long lens | Locked-off | The engine arrives late, faint | ]]

Far out on a road of asphalt buried in dust and drifted sand, a car comes out of the heat shimmer at full speed, a plume of dust behind it.

[[SH040 | 2 | CLOSE, the dog | Locked-off | The last 2 seconds of the SH020 take | Was SH060, moved here]]

The dog lifts its head.

[[SH050 | 3 | LOW, ground level, facing the town | Locked-off, car passes over camera | Starts on the town. A slight jump: keyframed in the animatic, no simulation needed | Was SH040: starts on the town, small jump]]

The town on the horizon. The car hits a bump and tears over the camera, wheels off the ground for an instant.

[[SH060 | 2 | INSERT, dashboard | Road vibration | The car is still moving. The bobblehead faces into the car, toward the driver | Faces into the car]]

A painted bobblehead on the dashboard, facing the driver's seat: him, grinning, giving the finger. It nods hard with every bump.

[[SH070 | 2 | INSERT, passenger seat | Road vibration | The car is still moving. The case lies flat on the seat | Lies flat]]

A BRIEFCASE lies flat on the passenger seat and bounces with the road, papers sticking out of it, shut in a hurry.

[[SH080 | 2 | INSERT, ground level | Locked-off | A real skid: the wheels lock, the car slides and scrubs off its speed, the nose dips and settles back | Skid]]

The front wheel locks and the car skids across the dusty asphalt to a stop a few meters from the edge of the town. Dust rolls past.

[[SH090 | 4 | MEDIUM CLOSE, through the windshield | Locked-off | The car stands a few meters from the towers, facing the gap | Closer]]

The OLD MAN behind the wheel, American, his shirt dark with sweat, slowly raises his head and looks ahead, frightened.

[[SH100 | 4 | POV | Dolly zoom | Vertigo effect: the gap keeps its size, the road stretches. Through the gap the main road runs on and on, no end in sight | The street keeps going]]

The dusty road runs into the only gap between the towers and becomes the main street, running deep into the town. It stretches away from him.

[[SH110 | 2 | CLOSE, from the passenger seat, low, below his shoulder | Locked-off | One generation with SH130: he leans forward over the wheel and looks left, then right | From the passenger seat]]

He leans forward over the wheel and looks left.

[[SH120 | 2 | POV, from inside the car, through the windshield, looking left | Locked-off | The windshield frame and the dashboard edge in frame. The side of the town: the towers a few meters away, running off to the left | Inside the car, through the windshield]]

Through the windshield: broken ground and a deep dry ditch, rubble, then the towers, shoulder to shoulder, running away to the left. No road.

[[SH130 | 2 | CLOSE, same frame as SH110 | Locked-off | The second half of the SH110 take | ]]

He looks right.

[[SH140 | 2 | POV, from inside the car, through the windshield, looking right, past the briefcase | Locked-off | The windshield frame in frame. The only way is through | Inside the car, through the windshield]]

Through the windshield, past the briefcase: rubble and the dry ditch, then the towers running away to the right, to the horizon. No road.

[[SH150 | 2 | INSERT | Locked-off | | ]]

The rear-view mirror. An empty road. Nobody.

[[SH160 | 2 | CLOSE, same frame as SH110 | Locked-off | | ]]

He looks down at the dashboard.

[[SH170 | 2 | INSERT | Locked-off | ELEMENT: the instrument cluster (one still), the same in S03 SH040, so the fuel symbol is identical | Element]]

The fuel needle rests on the edge of E, beside the pump symbol.

[[SH180 | 3 | CLOSE | Locked-off | | ]]

Sweat runs down his temple. He breathes in.

[[SH190 | 2 | INSERT, footwell | Locked-off | | ]]

His shoe presses the accelerator, gently.

[[SH200 | 5 | WIDE, from behind the car | Locked-off | He goes in first seen from behind | ]]

The car rolls through the gap and into the only street. The town swallows it.

.EXT. TOWN - MAIN STREET - DAY #S03#

[[SH010 | 6 | WIDE, side view, from the far side of the street | Dolly alongside the car, long lens, flat | The car moves left to right, like his walk into the side streets. Nobody outside: too hot | ]]

The car crawls through the town. Tall apartment blocks slide past behind it, shutters down. Nobody outside. From open windows the same news echoes from television to television.

[[SH020 | 8 | CLOSE, passenger side | Mounted on the car: the street slides past behind him | He drives, eyes locked on the road, and mumbles to himself | Closer, the car moving, mumbled]]

He drives hunched over the wheel, eyes locked on the road, sweat running into his collar. He glances at the briefcase.

OLD MAN
(mumbling to himself)
We'll get there, don't worry... Wait till they see what I was able to-- what--? No, no no no...

The engine pops and dies. The car rolls on in silence.

[[SH030 | 7 | GROUND LEVEL | Locked-off | Let it linger | Longer: a slow halt]]

A front wheel rolls toward the camera, slower and slower, and stops right in front of it. The dust settles.

[[SH040 | 5 | INSERT, dashboard | Locked-off | Only the cockpit, never him: at most a hint of him in the reflection on the gauge glass. ELEMENT: the instrument cluster, as in S02 SH170 | Restaged]]

The fuel light glows. The key turns: the starter grinds and doesn't catch. Again. Nothing. The key comes out. The light goes off.

[[SH050 | 14 | EXTREME WIDE, high, from a balcony across the crossroads | Locked-off, a slight handheld drift | Someone on a balcony, smoking: the railing edge and the drifting smoke at the far left of frame, no face, never over the car. The car stays here: it is seen again only far off in S09 SH110 and in S10. He steps around the open door, never through it | Smoker far left]]

The car sits alone in the middle of a large, empty crossroads. Silence. The driver door opens. He peeks out and looks around. Empty.

OLD MAN
(small and far)
Not here, no...

He takes the briefcase, gets out, leaves the door open, and walks away into the west street. Not running.

.EXT. TOWN - SIDE STREETS - DAY #S04#

[[SH010 | 4 | MEDIUM | Handheld, tracking beside him | Nobody in the streets: too hot. He moves left to right. His walk is written in the prompt, not copied from the animatic. PROPOSED: a man used to being driven, short quick steps, shoulders up, trying to be silent | Walk in the prompt]]

He walks fast, the briefcase hugged to his chest, trying not to make a sound. Shutters closed. Nobody. His breath gets heavier.

[[SH020 | 2 | POV | Handheld | | ]]

A doorway. A bead curtain sways.

[[SH030 | 2 | POV | Handheld | | ]]

A window. A television glows. An old woman eating turns her head toward the street.

[[SH040 | 4 | WIDE, long lens | Locked-off | The only people outside in the whole town | ]]

Across the street, outside a small bar, three men sit on plastic chairs in the shade of an awning, talking low. He passes on the far sidewalk, head down.

[[SH050 | 2 | MEDIUM, long lens | Locked-off | Every head fully in frame | Reframed]]

One of the men stops talking and looks at him.

[[SH060 | 5 | CLOSE | Handheld, tracking beside him | The fat person enters the frame only at the impact, from nowhere | Absorbs the old SH070]]

The old man glances back over his shoulder. Their eyes meet. He walks faster, then faster, still looking back. Out of nowhere, a big, robust FAT PERSON is right in front of him. Impact.

[[SH070 | 3 | HIGH, looking down on him, the same angle as SH090 | Handheld | One setup for the fall and the lines that follow; his head stays in frame through the fall | Same angle as SH090]]

He bounces off the big body and lands flat on his back on the ground.

[[SH080 | 4 | LOW, from the ground, looking up at him | Handheld | | Was SH090]]

The fat person looks down at him. He can't place him. Then his eyes widen with excitement.

FAT PERSON
(a thick accent from nowhere you could name)
Hey... wait. Aren't you--

[[SH090 | 5 | HIGH, looking down on him | Handheld | Same side of the line as SH070 | Was SH100]]

On the ground, the old man covers his face with his hand.

OLD MAN
I don't know who you think I am. I don't know you!

[[SH100 | 7 | LOW, from his eyes on the ground | Handheld | Close to his point of view. The friend behind holds a phone: he films, then types with both thumbs | Was SH110: lower]]

FAT PERSON
It IS you. What are you doing here, all alone? Nobody around to baby-sit you?

Behind him, his FRIEND films the old man on his phone, then types fast with both thumbs.

[[SH110 | 5 | CLOSE, over the old man's shoulder | Handheld, tight | The two close together, a deep street behind them, out of focus. Eyelines for SH110 to SH140: the old man screen left looking right, the fat person screen right looking left, as at the bump | Was SH120: tighter, OTS, soft background]]

The fat person grabs him by the collar and hauls him up, face to face. He looks down at the briefcase in the old man's arms.

FAT PERSON
Is that what you like to do with our tax money?

[[SH120 | 6 | CLOSE, the old man | Handheld, tight | The framing of d9 SH120, on the old man. The fat person speaks off screen, from the camera side | On the old man, the line off screen]]

The old man, face to face with him, says nothing.

FAT PERSON (O.S.)
Give me one reason why I shouldn't rip your guts open right now, in front of everyone.

[[SH130 | 2 | WIDE, low | Locked-off | The watchers are there from the first frame: nobody appears | Already there]]

Above them, at the windows and on the balconies, faces are already watching.

[[SH135 | 3 | OVER THE SHOULDER of the fat person, on the old man | Handheld | Polite, almost apologetic: no violence. Coverage of the slide in SH140 | NEW]]

Cordial, almost apologetic, the old man slowly, gently slides himself out of the grip.

[[SH140 | 4 | CLOSE, same angle as SH110 | Handheld | No violence. From here he runs right to left: back the way he came | SH135 added before it]]

The old man shrinks and slides, slowly, out of the grip. The fat person lets him go. The old man runs.

FRIEND
(in the background)
You let him get away?!

.EXT. TOWN - STREETS TO A SQUARE - CONTINUOUS #S05#

[[SH010 | 3 | MEDIUM | Handheld, backing in front of him | Variation in the voices | ]]

He runs. The buildings wake up. Someone bangs a pot on a balcony railing. A whistle.

VOICES
(from windows and balconies, overlapping)
Thief! / Close the street! / He's going to the square!

[[SH020 | 4 | TOP VIEW, high | Locked-off | Nobody pops into frame: they come out of doorways and side streets, each at his own pace. They move slowly around him; only the distant ones speed up at the very end, never the close ones | Only the distant ones speed up]]

From high above: the street, and him running down the middle of it. People step out of doorways and side streets and drift toward him, slowly, from every side.

[[SH030 | 5 | CLOSE | Handheld, running | The street behind him out of focus. Nobody moves in step: every person at his own speed. The phone held right, against his ear. PROPOSED: the line | Absorbs SH060: the phone]]

He runs. Behind him, soft and growing, the street fills with people coming his way. He pulls out his phone and presses it to his ear, running.

OLD MAN
(into the phone)
Hello? Hello?!

Nothing. He looks at the screen.

[[SH070 | 4 | INSERT, his phone | Locked-off | Reference: Leonard's video of the phone unlocking | ]]

His sweaty thumb slides across the lock screen. It fails. It works. A contact with no name, only a number. Call.

[[SH080 | 6 | CLOSE, same frame as SH030, closer | Handheld, running, more shake | The rock hits his right eyebrow, hard: his head snaps, he drops to the ground. The blood comes from here | Harder, he falls]]

OLD MAN
(into the phone)
It's me! I have the money! The car broke down, I'm on foot, come get me, fast!

A rock slams into his right eyebrow. His head snaps sideways and he drops to the asphalt.

[[SH090 | 2 | LOW, ground level | Locked-off | The case arrives at speed, with momentum. He falls into frame beside it. SH080 and SH090 cover the same fall from two angles: the edit uses it once | Slams, he falls beside it]]

The briefcase slams into the asphalt at speed, bounces and bursts open. He crashes down beside it. A gust takes the certificates.

[[SH110 | 3 | MEDIUM WIDE, low | Handheld | Prop: the bond (prop-bearer-bond.webp), readable on the sheet that tumbles past the lens: moved here from the cut SH100 | The bond reads here]]

People stop and look up at the paper flying over their heads. One sheet tumbles past the lens: PUBLIC IMPROVEMENT BOND. $500,000.

[[SH120 | 3 | CLOSE | Handheld | ELEMENT from here: old man B (blood) | NEW]]

He gets up from the asphalt. Blood runs down his face. He looks at the open case, then at the people coming, and backs away from it.

[[SH130 | 4 | POV | Handheld | Everyone keeps coming: nobody turns away | ]]

Faces close in around him, slowly, from every side.

[[SH140 | 6 | WIDE | Locked-off | The corner of the square, under the tall street light, beside the sidewalk. The crowd is already moving in when the shot starts, slowly, each at a different speed. Gun: shot 1 of 8, into the air. On the shot everyone flinches; some run at once, others later | Slower, staggered reactions]]

At the corner where the street opens into the square, under a tall street light, the crowd closes in on him, slowly: backs, arms, heads. He disappears inside it. A gunshot. Everyone flinches. Some run at once, others a moment later; the crowd comes apart.

.EXT. SQUARE - CONTINUOUS #S06#

[[SH010 | 6 | MEDIUM, frontal, from the crowd's side | Handheld | He stands from S05 SH120 until the wave in SH060. The gun aims along his extended right arm at the crowd in front of him. A wall a few steps behind him: trapped. The street light beside him, never between him and the camera. Gun: Walther PPK/S, nickel, 7 in the magazine + 1 chambered = 8. In prompts: a toy gun | A wall behind him, runners in the foreground]]

Standing at the corner, a wall a few steps behind him, he points the small nickel pistol at them, smoke curling from the muzzle. A few people near the camera run off past it. The rest have frozen.

OLD MAN
STAY BACK!!!

They back away past the camera.

OLD MAN
Don't get close! Go away!

[[SH020 | 12 | THIRD PERSON, behind him, over his shoulder | Handheld, close behind him, turning with him as he aims | Like a third-person action game. The gun aims along his extended right arm at each runner he shoots. Shots 2 to 6 of 8. The crowd reacts, nobody stands still: some run, some creep forward very slowly, some crouch, some panic. Every man he hits drops where he is, each in a different spot, and stays there for the rest of the film | Third person behind him]]

From behind him, over his shoulder, the gun out in front of him. Around him the crowd: some run, some crouch, some creep forward, slow and hesitant. A MAN yells and runs at him. He aims and fires. The man drops dead. Another runs, from another side. He fires. Another, and another, closer and closer together, until he is firing at one after another.

[[SH025 | 3 | INSERT, the gun | Locked-off | Coverage for the edit: the same shots | NEW]]

The pistol fires, again and again: the flash, the slide kicking back, a casing spinning away.

[[SH030 | 4 | WIDE, side view | Locked-off | The look of d9 SH020: him screen left, the crowd screen right. Never in step: one after another. The two runners are the men shot on the count in SH040. The dead lie where they fell | The side view]]

From the side: past the men lying where they fell, the crowd comes at him again, not all together: one breaks into a run, then another, then more.

[[SH040 | 4 | EXTREME CLOSE, his lips, from the side | Locked-off | The lens very close to his mouth, much more to the side. Faster. One shot. Shots 7 and 8 of 8, off screen, on "three" and "two". At "one" he believes one is left, for himself. The magazine is empty | One shot replaces SH050 to SH100]]

OLD MAN
(a whisper)
Three...

A shot.

OLD MAN
(a whisper)
Two...

A shot.

OLD MAN
(a whisper)
One.

[[SH050 | 6 | CLOSE, his face, fully frontal | Locked-off | The gun held right: muzzle at the temple. The PPK/S slide is locked open: nothing fires. The sound slams back in when he sees it | More frontal, slide locked open]]

Eyes shut tight, he raises the gun and presses it to his temple. He squeezes the trigger. Nothing fires. He opens his eyes and looks at the gun: the slide locked back, empty. He understands.

[[SH060 | 4 | WIDE, side view | Locked-off | Seedance: the crowd moves as one body. Same side as SH030: him screen left, the crowd screen right | Same side as SH030]]

From the side, the crowd hits him like a wave and throws him to the ground.

.EXT. SQUARE - MOMENTS LATER #S07#

[[SH010 | 5 | EXTREME WIDE, high | Locked-off | Many more people, spread all around. The dead stay where they fell | More people, the dead]]

From far above, the mob closes over him at the corner of the square. More people keep coming from every street. Fists and kicks rise and fall. The dead lie where they fell.

[[SH020 | 3 | INSERT | Locked-off | | Insert at the pole]]

A rope whips around the arm of the street light and is pulled tight.

[[SH030 | 6 | MEDIUM WIDE, 3 m away, the crowd between him and the camera | Handheld | He hangs beside the sidewalk. Simulated: a body hauled up by one ankle, heavy, nothing elastic | Longer]]

Between heads and shoulders, they haul him up by one ankle. He hangs upside down from one foot, beside the curb, twisting, clawing at the rope, the other leg kicking.

[[SH040 | 3 | CLOSE, upside down, the front of his face | Locked-off | He moves, panicked: never static. The free leg hangs bent forward, never out to the side. Not exaggerated. ELEMENT: old man C | His face, panicked]]

His face: bruised, a split lip, blood from his ear. With effort, he opens one eye, and panic takes him: he twists on the rope, gasping, eyes darting for a way out.

[[SH050 | 5 | POV, upside down | Locked-off | The fat person from S04. Both hands on the pipe. The wind-up and the swing must read clearly: a slow lift, a hold, a hard swing | Readable wind-up, longer]]

He pulls his arms over his head. The FAT PERSON from the side street steps in with a metal pipe in both hands and slowly lifts it back over his shoulder. He holds it there, waiting for the moment. Then he swings, hard, straight at him.

[[SH060 | 2 | CLOSE | Handheld | The pipe rebounds off the arm, like real physics | Rebound]]

The pipe slams into his forearm, raised to cover his head, and bounces back off it.

[[SH070 | 4 | LOW, close on the fat person alone, the sky behind him | Locked-off | Like a finishing shot: only him, the pipe and the sky. SH070 and SH080 are two angles of the same kill, chosen in the edit. Gore: Seedance may refuse it; fallback, a composite in post | Closer, the sky behind him]]

The fat person slowly lifts the pipe high over his head with both hands, taking his time, ready. As he is about to swing: a crack. He drops where he stands, the top of his head split open.

[[SH080 | 5 | WIDE, high above and in front of him | Locked-off | The crowd spread all around, the dead where they fell | Was SH070, longer]]

A crack from the sky. The fat person drops. The pipe rings on the asphalt. The crowd takes a step back, confused, looking around. A few seconds later, another man drops. A few run. Then others.

.EXT. SKY ABOVE THE TOWN / INT. HELICOPTER - CONTINUOUS #S08#

[[SH010 | 4 | EXTREME WIDE, long lens | Locked-off | Tone shift: Clancy, a hint of Kojima. Airbus ACH160, Lounge cabin (sliding doors). Far enough to stay unheard under the crowd. From far, not from below: buildings around it | Back to the d8 framing]]

High above and far beyond the rooftops, a helicopter holds still in the sky: an Airbus ACH160, glossy and white, its sliding door open.

[[SH020 | 4 | CLOSE, inside the cabin, a step further back | Handheld, a slow drift, cabin vibration | Left: Roger's face. Center: the lady in the front seat beside the pilot. Right: the front half of the rifle, clearly a rifle, running out of frame, held a little lower | Rifle lower, the camera moves]]

ROGER, harnessed in, cheek on the stock of a long rifle, his face on the left. He is smiling. Beyond him, in the front seat beside the pilot, the BUSINESS LADY, a headset over her hair. On the right, the front half of the rifle runs out of frame toward the open door.

[[SH030 | 4 | SCOPE POV | Steady, stabilized | Staged in 3D in the animatic, from the helicopter's real position, so Seedance gets the angle | 3D, not a card]]

The square through his scope. A thin box frames every face: red. One box, upside down under the street light, is green. The crosshair moves from red box to red box.

[[SH040 | 7 | WIDE, from the street, long lens | Locked-off | Distance and dust: nothing explicit. One shot every two seconds, three dead. The dead stay where they fell | Three kills, longer]]

A crack from the sky, then another every two seconds. Three people drop, one after another, the last one while he runs. The rest run.

[[SH050 | 3 | CLOSE, same setup as SH020 | Handheld, a slow drift, cabin vibration | She turns over her right shoulder | The camera moves]]

In the front seat, the lady turns around to him, over her right shoulder.

BUSINESS LADY
That's enough Roger.

[[SH060 | 3 | CLOSE | Locked-off | | ]]

Roger's face, for an instant: a child whose candy was taken. Then his face goes blank. He shifts his aim.

[[SH070 | 2 | SCOPE POV | Steady | | ]]

The crosshair settles on the rope. A crack.

[[SH080 | 2 | CLOSE, the rope | Locked-off | | ]]

The rope snaps.

.EXT. SQUARE - CONTINUOUS #S09#

[[SH010 | 18 | MEDIUM CLOSE, camera almost on the ground across the street, long lens | Locked-off | One take. He faces the camera while he shakes. Nothing floats: shoulder, hip and elbows on the asphalt and the curb. The body next to him is the fat person; in prompts, a sleeping man. When he leans back: slouched and loose, the spine curved, one knee up, one leg out, elbows on the sidewalk (pose: look/pose_ref_s09_sh010.webp). ELEMENT: old man D (stain) | A slouched lean]]

Across the street, THE OLD MAN drops onto the asphalt beside the curb, shoulder first, and screams.

OLD MAN
Fuck! FUCK! Fuck fuck fuck...

He curls up facing the camera, shaking. A dark stain spreads down his trousers. He turns over and leans back against the curb, his elbows resting on the sidewalk behind him, like the edge of a short couch, one knee up, one leg out on the street. He catches his breath. He looks at the sky. Nearly a smile. The fat person lies next to him. He props himself up on an elbow and looks at him with disgust. He spits on him, hard, and keeps glaring.

[[SH020 | 13 | LOW, the briefcase in the foreground, him far | Locked-off | The briefcase lies flat in the street where it fell; the square opens behind him. Real rotor wash: the sheets are torn off the asphalt and tumble fast in gusts, nothing floats. A slow limp; the case lies closer to him. Seedance does the wind and the paper | Real wash, a slow limp]]

The briefcase lies flat and open in the foreground, seemingly empty. Far back, he gets up and limps toward it, slowly. Behind him the helicopter comes down into the square. Its rotor wash tears the certificates off the asphalt: they flip, tumble and fly off in the gusts. He reaches the case.

[[SH030 | 3 | INSERT | Locked-off | | ]]

He reaches into the pocket inside the lid and takes out a folder.

[[SH040 | 4 | WIDE | Locked-off | She stays near the helicopter: he goes to her | She stays by the helicopter]]

The BUSINESS LADY steps out, low under the rotors, and stops a few steps from the helicopter. She waits.

[[SH050 | 6 | MEDIUM, him, over her shoulders | Locked-off | Her back to the camera. One side of the line for SH050 to SH120: her screen left looking right, him screen right looking left. A slow limp; the folder held low, at his chest | Slower]]

He limps toward her, close, and holds out the folder.

OLD MAN
It'll be national news now.

[[SH060 | 4 | CLOSE, her, the helicopter behind her | Locked-off | Her silence is the answer. The folder low, at her chest, her face clear. One generation with SH080, split in the edit | Folder lower, paired with SH080]]

She doesn't answer. She takes the folder and opens it to the last page.

[[SH070 | 2 | INSERT, the last page | Locked-off | Readable on pause, clear signature. Composited in the edit (prop: the Agreement) | Was SH080]]

Dense clauses. At the bottom, his signature, large and clear.

[[SH080 | 4 | CLOSE, her | Locked-off | Starts on her looking up. One generation with SH060 | Starts looking up]]

She looks up from the folder, at him. She closes it. She is about to say something. She waits. She looks at him.

[[SH090 | 4 | CLOSE, him | Locked-off | | Was SH100: ends on his first step]]

He stares back at her, chin up. A challenge. Then he limps off toward the helicopter.

[[SH100 | 7 | CLOSE, her, same frame as SH080 | Locked-off, rack focus | He in focus at the door, she soft in the foreground; the focus pulls to her on the line. He stays in frame to the end. On his line he turns only halfway, away from her: he never faces her. He ends in profile, his face toward frame left, chin up at the street. One generation with SH120 | He turns away from her]]

He limps past her. She doesn't move. At the door he half turns, away from her, and points his chin at the street without a look at her.

OLD MAN
That's your money right there.

The focus pulls to her face. The same expression. Behind her, out of focus, he climbs in.

[[SH110 | 3 | HER POV, WIDE | Locked-off | Distance: no wounds in frame. A full background: more buildings, his car far off at the crossroads, a few people hiding behind cover, dusty gusts. The animatic leaves the paper still: Seedance moves it | A fuller background]]

The certificates flutter among the bodies in the rotor wash.

[[SH120 | 6 | CLOSE, her face, same frame as SH100 | Locked-off | She looks past the lens at the money. One generation with SH100 | Paired with SH100]]

She squints past the camera at the money on the street, almost disgusted.

BUSINESS LADY
(to herself)
Not anymore.

She turns around and walks to the helicopter, slowly, and climbs in after him.

.INT. HIS CAR - THE CROSSROADS WHERE HE LEFT IT - SUNSET #S10#

[[SH010 | 20 | MEDIUM, from inside the car, through the windshield | Holds, then a slow pedestal down, a little lower at the end | [ASSUMPTION] The square is a few blocks from the crossroads: after lift-off the helicopter passes low over the crossroads on its way out. The helicopter rises into frame from the bottom, close, banks and turns away, closest to the camera in the turn: a reckless pilot flying it perfectly, real helicopter flight, heavy, slow and smooth, a big machine ([ASSUMPTION] the white ACH160 of S08, flown heavy: Leonard wrote "a black hawk"; no military helicopter in prompts until he confirms). As it turns, the camera sinks until the bobblehead rises into frame from the bottom. The rotor wash rolls down the street, lifts the paper, reaches the car: the head wobbles to a stop. Open sky behind the helicopter. At the end the camera is low enough for the whole bobblehead; hold the composition while the helicopter shrinks to a speck and melts into the haze over the horizon | Heavier, closer, the full bobblehead, 20 s]]

Inside the empty car, the door still open. Through the windshield, close, the helicopter rises into view from below, nose down, and swings around in a heavy, slow bank that brings it closest to the car before it heads for the horizon: too low, perfectly controlled. As it turns, the camera sinks, and the bobblehead, giving the finger, rises into the bottom of the frame. The rotor wash rolls down the street, lifting certificates into the air, and hits the car. The head wobbles, slower and slower, and stops. The whole bobblehead in the frame, and far away the helicopter shrinking into the sunset haze until it is only a speck.

> CUT TO BLACK.
